@* Tooltip's Overview, written by hand after Popover's: icon buttons with shortcuts (previewed
   in each mode), then placement. Accessibility (what the trigger needs, what a tooltip can't
   hold) and See also come from the doc comment. *@

<TextBlock>A tooltip is a short hint about a control that shows on hover and on keyboard focus. It suits what an icon does, or its shortcut. For a panel the user clicks to open, with links or a form, use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/popover">Popover</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Icon buttons and shortcuts</Heading>
<TextBlock>An icon button shows only an icon, so a tooltip says what it does. Wrap the button in a <Code>Tooltip</Code> and set <Code>Text</Code>. For markup, such as a keyboard shortcut in a <Anchor Href="docs/components/kbd">Kbd</Anchor>, set <Code>Content</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tooltip-usage" />
<TextBlock>A hover waits 300 milliseconds before the tooltip shows; to change that, set <Code>Delay</Code>. Keyboard focus shows it at once.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>Inside a tooltip, an <Anchor Href="docs/components/icon-button">IconButton</Anchor> leaves out its own <Code>title</Code>, so hovering shows one tooltip, not two. The IconButton still requires its <Code>Label</Code>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Placement</Heading>
<TextBlock>A tooltip shows above its trigger by default. To show it below, before or after the trigger, set <Code>Placement</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tooltip-sides" />
<TextBlock>With <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">IzzyBlazor's script</Anchor>, a tooltip with no room on its side, such as above a button at the top of the window, shows on the opposite side. With JavaScript off, it keeps its side.</TextBlock>

